Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 06:40:55 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 10/13] Windows 0.8.0: only the native plug-in + ASIO; the
 Access files are unpacked, not installed; earlier installs cleaned up

User test of rc3 (2026-10-15): the classic plug-in and its ASIO device next to the new ones were confusing.
- MSI: no classic plug-in "Virus TI (TI Revive)", no ASIO wrapper, no Control Center launcher (an upgrade removes
  them); Start menu "Set up Access Virus TI files"; Access' Control Center shortcuts back to plain on install
- tirevive-access.ps1: the Access .msi is unpacked (msiexec /a: no custom actions, no drivers) and only Virus
  Control.dll, firmware.bin, the manuals (Program Files\Access Music\Virus TI) and the factory patch libraries
  (Documents, only missing files) are copied; a full Access installation of earlier TI Revive versions is offered
  for removal (its needed files and the patch libraries stay, its dead ASIO entry goes); one UAC prompt
Tested in the win11 VM: upgrade over 0.8.0-rc + 0.7.x leftovers (classic plug-in, ASIO wrapper, test folder gone),
setup.exe replaces the 0.7.1 bundle entry, Access removal (product, original plug-in, Start menu entries, ASIO
entry gone; 96 patch files kept), extraction from scratch (files + manuals, no product, no drivers), the extracted
DLL loads (vtimodel: 587 parameters, 438 images, 26 ROM banks).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
